  <h1 id="C6" style="text-align:center">Welcome to The World of Fashion History</h1>

  <marquee behaviour="scroll" direction="left">EXPLORE key moments that shaped what we wear — from ancient drapes to digital couture!</marquee>

  <h2>Ancient Civilizations</h2>
  <p>Learn how Egyptians, Greeks, and Romans used draped garments, linen, and wool — setting foundations for silhouette and status.
     Here's a link about <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clothing_in_ancient_Egypt">ancient Egyptian dress</a>.</p>

  <h2>Renaissance to Baroque</h2>
  <p>Sumptuous fabrics, corsetry, ruffs, and courtly display defined European fashion.
     Read more in this overview of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_fashion_design#Renaissance">Renaissance period</a>.</p>

  <h2>19th-Century Tailoring</h2>
  <p>Industrialization brought sewing machines, department stores, and precise tailoring.
     Explore the era of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victorian_fashion">Victorian silhouette</a>.</p>

  <h2>20th-Century Revolutions</h2>
  <p>From Chanel’s modernism to Dior’s New Look, youth culture, and street style—fashion accelerated with media and mass-production.</p>
  <h2>Click the image to learn about haute couture:</h2>
